    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Okay, fine. Let's stay general then. If a group of people were suddenly being monitored and needed to send subtle signals through standard corporate jargon without alerting the \"observer,\" what kind of linguistic markers or tactical shifts would they use to maintain a baseline while still signaling something to an insider? Like, if you were trying to communicate a change in status or a warning through everyday email phrasing, how would that look compared to normal business communications?",
